{"name":"Roman Purple","hex":"#524765","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roman","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Upright, as opposed to italic.","Of or related to the Latin alphabet or roman numerals."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the main three types used for the Latin alphabet (the others being italics and blackletter), in which the ascenders are mostly straight.","Ellipsis of roman numeral."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roman"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fuchsia (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Fuchsia is a vivid pinkish–red color, named after the color of the flower of the fuchsia plant, which was named by a French botanist, Charles Plumier, after the 16th-century German botanist Leonhart Fuchs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/DoubleFuchsias_wb.jpg/330px-DoubleFuchsias_wb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuchsia_(color)","wikidata":"Q5005364"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Basic_Fuchsine_in_aqueous_solution.jpg/120px-Basic_Fuchsine_in_aqueous_solution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Basic_Fuchsine_in_aqueous_solution.jpg/250px-Basic_Fuchsine_in_aqueous_solution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Basic_Fuchsine_in_aqueous_solution.jpg/120px-Basic_Fuchsine_in_aqueous_solution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABasic_Fuchsine_in_aqueous_solution.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Basic_Fuchsine_Crystals.JPG/120px-Basic_Fuchsine_Crystals.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Basic_Fuchsine_Crystals.JPG/250px-Basic_Fuchsine_Crystals.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Basic_Fuchsine_Crystals.JPG/120px-Basic_Fuchsine_Crystals.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABasic_Fuchsine_Crystals.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/RGB_illumination.jpg/330px-RGB_illumination.jpg?utm_source=